        "original_id": "f3c7f4fd-f536-551a-87a9-7202306980c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Courtenay, John Mills, Robert Emmet Smith\n- Films: King Rat, The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner, Billy Liar, Doctor Zhivago\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Art Direction, knighthood\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Courtenay was born on 25 February 1937 and is an English actor.\n- Tom Courtenay came to prominence in the early 1960s through the films The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner (1962), Billy Liar (1963), and Doctor Zhivago (1965).\n- Tom Courtenay received a knighthood in February 2001 for services to cinema and theatre.\n- John Mills and Tom Courtenay were among the supporting cast of the film King Rat.\n- Robert Emmet Smith was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Art Direction for the film King Rat.",
